# The workhorses hosts file: copy it to ~/.config/workhorses/hosts and edit it.
# One host per line: name, ssh target, arch, cores, RAM in GB, then any host options.
# - name: lower-case letters, digits and dashes, and not ps or stop; wh and sync.sh take it as the host's name.
# - ssh target: an alias from ~/.ssh/config or user@host. ~/.ssh/config decides the route.
# - arch: x86_64 or arm64. cores and RAM: whole numbers, shown to Claude in the host table.
# - A Linux host, WSL2 on a Windows PC included, takes the same five fields and no options:
#   sync.sh refuses options on a host that runs Linux. Its work copies stay under ~/work on the
#   Linux filesystem, never under /mnt/c.
# - options: none by default. Each changes the Mac for every user of it, so give them only to a Mac
#   that exists to run jobs. sync.sh applies them; removing one later undoes nothing.
#     autologin      log the workhorse user in at boot; stores its password in /etc/kcpassword
#     dock           trim the Dock to Terminal, Activity Monitor and System Settings
#     firewall       macOS firewall on, in stealth mode, signed apps allowed
#     git-identity   a neutral global git name and email for test suites that commit
#     headless       no screensaver and no Siri
#     key-only-ssh   ssh logins by key only
#     maxfiles       raise the open-file limit to 65536/200000, now and at every boot
#     no-sleep       never sleep; restart after a power cut; wake on LAN
#     no-spotlight   Spotlight indexing off on every volume
#     screensharing  let the workhorse user in over Screen Sharing
#     tailscale      install Tailscale (log in on the Mac's screen)
#     wallpaper=NAME a solid-colour wallpaper from /System/Library/Desktop Pictures/Solid Colors,
#                    with _ for each space: wallpaper=Turquoise_Green
#     wifi-off       Wi-Fi off while Ethernet is up, so traffic takes the cable
#   All but dock, git-identity, headless and wallpaper need sudo, so sync.sh asks your
#   sudo-password helper for a host that has one.
# The first host listed wins a tie when wh picks one by load.
alpha  alpha-mini             x86_64  6   16  no-sleep maxfiles headless wallpaper=Turquoise_Green
beta   beta-mini              x86_64  6   16  no-sleep maxfiles headless wallpaper=Electric_Blue
gamma  me@gamma.example.test  arm64   10  16
